    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d840">

                <pb facs="1038" n="1028" xml:id="pg1028"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">893.6359/11–2247: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Acting Secretary of State
                        to the Ambassador in China</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                            >Stuart</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1947-11-22T17:00:00-05:00">November 22,
                            1947—5 p.m.</date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>1421. Revised draft submitted your telegram 2265<anchor n="20" xml:id="d840-f1"/>
                    now under consideration. Department and AEC much appreciate work done by Embassy
                    and Keiser in this matter.</p>
                <p>AEC believes that consideration of draft and any further steps in implementation
                    of it would be facilitated by Keiser’s presence here and his direct return
                    travel is therefore authorized as soon as practicable without waiting for the
                    Generalissimo’s reaction.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Lovett</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
